# Generated into src/Makevars by ./configure (and src/Makevars.win by
# ./configure.win). Do not edit the generated file: it is .gitignore'd and
# rewritten on every install.
#
# The include path for <zucrypt.h> is NOT set here. R adds <pkg>/include for
# every LinkingTo package to CLINK_CPPFLAGS, so "LinkingTo: zucrypt" in
# DESCRIPTION is what puts the header on the path. And no define is needed to
# match zucrypt's build: zucrypt.h names no backend type, which is the reason
# no upstream header is installed (zucrypt design.md section 8.3).
#
# $(C_VISIBILITY): this package's own functions stay out of its dynamic
# symbol table except R_init_zucryptlink, as a careful consumer would build.
# The archive's objects were compiled hidden by zucrypt already; whether they
# stay out of this shared object's exports is what tools/check-linking.sh
# audits.
PKG_CFLAGS = $(C_VISIBILITY)

# Single-quoted: the path comes from system.file(), so it sits under the R
# library, and a library path containing a space -- the norm on Windows,
# where the user library lives under the profile directory -- would otherwise
# reach the linker as two nonexistent arguments. tools/check-linking.sh
# installs into a library whose path contains a space to hold this.
PKG_LIBS = '@ZUCRYPT_LIB@/libzucrypt.a'
